    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106102" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τύχων</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχη</span>) a name of Hermes, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Inscr.Magn.</u>
			203
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Theognost.
			<u>Can.</u>
			33
		</span></i>; of Priapus, <i><span class="en">
			D.S.
			4.6
		</span></i> (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τυφῶνα</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; [Πρίαπος] ἔοικε . . Τύχωνι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					13.1.12
				</span></i>
			; defined as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμων περὶ τὴν
				Ἀφροδίτην,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
				<u>in Theod.</u>
				1.274
			</span></i> H.; he is the giver of small gifts to mortals, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.334
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pers.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Apolloph.
				1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> name of the deified lance
			of Alexander of Pherae, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pel.</u>
				29
			</span></i>.</div>
